# 🚀 RAG System — Built From Scratch

A fully modular **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)** system built in Python for learning and experimentation.

This project breaks down every component of a RAG pipeline into clear, independent modules — so you understand *how it works under the hood*, not just how to use it.

---

## 📂 Project Structure


rag_sys/
├── ingestion.py # Load documents from disk
├── chunker.py # Split text into chunks
├── embedder.py # Convert text → embeddings
├── vector_store.py # Store & search vectors (ChromaDB)
├── retriever.py # (legacy) basic semantic retrieval
├── generator.py # Prompt construction + LLM call
├── pipeline.py # End-to-end pipeline
│
├── hybrid/ # 🔥 Hybrid retrieval (BM25 + vector)
│ ├── bm25_index.py
│ ├── hybrid_retriever.py
│ ├── hybrid_pipeline.py
│ └── evaluate_hybrid.py
│
├── cli.py # Command-line interface
└── requirements.txt

data/
└── sample_docs/ # Example documents


---

## ⚡ Quickstart

### 1. Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
2. Set API key (for LLM)
export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_key_here
# OR
export OPENAI_API_KEY=your_key_here
3. Ingest documents
python -m rag_sys.cli ingest --dir data/sample_docs
4. Ask questions
python -m rag_sys.cli query --question "What is self-attention?"
5. Run evaluation
python -m rag_sys.cli evaluate
6. Run hybrid evaluation
python -m rag_sys.cli evaluate_hybrid
🧠 Architecture
Ingestion (offline)
Documents
   ↓
Chunker
   ↓
Embedder
   ↓
Vector Store
Query (online)
Query
  ↓
Embedder
  ↓
Retriever (Vector / Hybrid)
  ↓
Top-k Chunks
  ↓
Generator (LLM)
  ↓
Answer
🔍 Hybrid Retrieval (Key Feature)

This system supports Hybrid Search:

🔤 BM25 → keyword matching
🧠 Embeddings → semantic understanding
🔗 RRF → combines both rankings

Why it matters:

Query Type	Best Method
Exact terms	BM25
Conceptual	Embeddings
Real-world	Hybrid ✅
⚖️ Key Trade-offs
Chunk Size
Small	Large
More precise	More context
Less context	Possible noise

👉 Recommended: 300–500 chars

Overlap
Low	High
Clean chunks	Better continuity
May cut meaning	Slight duplication

👉 Recommended: 10–20%

Embedding Models
Model	Notes
all-MiniLM-L6-v2	Fast baseline
all-mpnet-base-v2	Higher quality
BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5	🔥 Best for retrieval
📊 Evaluation

Run:

python -m rag_sys.cli evaluate

Metrics:

Precision@k → how relevant results are
Recall@k → did we find the right doc
Top-1 Accuracy → is the best chunk correct
🛠 Improving Retrieval
1. Better embeddings
embedding_model="BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5"
2. Query formatting (important for BGE)
"Represent this sentence for searching relevant passages: " + query
3. Hybrid search

Already implemented in:

rag_sys/hybrid/
4. Reranking (next step)

Use a cross-encoder to re-rank top-k results for higher precision.

⚠️ Common Failure Modes
Problem	Cause
Wrong answer	Wrong chunk retrieved
Mixed concepts	Chunk too large
Missed answer	Chunk too small
Hallucination	Weak context
📈 Scaling to Production
Area	Dev	Production
Vector DB	ChromaDB	Pinecone / Qdrant
Embeddings	Local CPU	GPU service
Retrieval	Single stage	Hybrid + rerank
Eval	Manual	Automated (RAGAS)
🧪 Future Improvements
 Add cross-encoder reranker
 Streaming responses
 Async pipeline
 API layer (FastAPI)
 UI (Streamlit / React)
📚 References
RAG Paper: https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.08909
RAGAS: https://github.com/explodinggradients/ragas
Sentence Transformers: https://sbert.net/
ChromaDB: https://docs.trychroma.com/
💡 Why this project?

Most RAG tutorials hide complexity.

This project shows:

how chunking affects retrieval
how embeddings actually behave
why hybrid search is necessary
how evaluation reveals real issues
🧑‍💻 Author

Built for learning, debugging, and understanding RAG systems deeply.


